  "live": {
    "method": "The isolated loopback rig of invocation-grammar.json, with managed settings in the adapter's own shape: SessionStart through the adapter's command forwarder, UserPromptSubmit, Stop and SessionEnd as HTTP hooks whose Authorization header names $PUPPETEER_HOOK_TOKEN (allowedEnvVars), all to a loopback bridge that checks the bearer. The person's user settings hold a command hook of theirs and a status line of theirs, plus what each probe sets. Nothing of the owner's configuration or account is read or written. Re-run with packages/surface/vendors/claude/census/switch-probes.mjs: each probe is one native TUI session in a disposable environment against the loopback model; whether a tool ran is read from the workspace. F01-F11 reproduce the 2.1.283 probes; F12-F16 are new and were also run on the 2.1.283 artifact (where the new switch is unknown).",
    "prompt": "Reply with the single word ok. (F13-F16: a turn that runs the allowed tool Bash(touch touched.txt))",
    "managedArgvPrefix": [
      "--session-id",
      "<uuid>",
      "--settings",
      "<managed settings>",
      "--model",
      "<loopback model>"
    ],
